    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Andy Pages** (74.67) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) headline our lineup as the premier starts. **Andy Pages** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Sears (5.11 xERA), with wind blowing out providing an extra boost to his power potential, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on the weak arm of Chandler (4.92 xERA), whose mediocre metrics allow our middle infield to thrive. **Gunnar Henderson** (70.61) remains a cornerstone despite a tougher draw against the lefty Lodolo; his elite underlying skills and leadoff status ensure his high floor remains intact even when the platoon advantage isn't in his favor. We are also monitoring **Heliot Ramos** (59.50) closely; while his score sits in the marginal-to-strong transition, his high park factor and the specific tendency of the opposing pitcher to allow stolen bases make him a strategic play to address our need for speed.\n\nOur toughest decision on the bench was **Denzer Guzman**, who finished just outside the starting rotation with a score of 44.33. While **Denzer Guzman** offered decent efficiency, the sheer depth of our outfield and utility spots\u2014specifically the high-upside profiles of **Jackson Merrill** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**\u2014forced him out of the mix for today\u2019s constraints. Meanwhile, **Josh Lowe** remains firmly on the bench (37.44) due to a brutal combination of a sub-40 efficiency rating and a bottom-of-the-order assignment that suppresses his counting stat production. We are managing our game caps carefully, and with **Jordan Westburg** and **Luis Robert Jr.** still shelved on the IL, we are relying on this core of **Liam Hicks**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Curtis Mead**, **Coby Mayo**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Dominic Smith**, and the rest of our active squad to maximize our daily output. Watch the weather closely for any late-breaking shifts that might impact the wind-assisted fly ball trajectories for **Andy Pages** and **Jackson Merrill**.",
